regulator: qcom-rpmh: add PMXR2230 regulator support

Add the PMXR2230 PMIC (SPMI id "b" on the Retroid Pocket G2 / SM8635 Cliffs)
to the grouped RPMh regulator driver: a pmxr2230_vreg_data[] table and the
matching "qcom,pmxr2230-rpmh-regulators" of_device_id.

The regulator complement (3 FTSMPS, LDOs l1-l5/l7-l13/l16-l23, BOB1) and each
rail's operating window were read from the G2's own /proc/device-tree dump
(dumps/g2/g2-devicetree-20260914-*). Each rail is mapped to the mainline
pmic5 hardware-range struct whose window covers it:
  - smps1-3        -> pmic5_ftsmps525 (0.3-1.3V + 1.376V+; covers s1 ~2.0V,
                      s2 ~1.4V, s3 ~1.0V)
  - ldo1-5,7-12    -> pmic5_nldo515   (0.32-2.0V; incl. the 1.8V rails, as
                      pm8550 also does)
  - ldo13,16-23    -> pmic5_pldo      (1.504-3.544V; incl. the SD rails l13
                      = vmmc and l23 = vqmmc)
  - bob1           -> pmic5_bob       (3.0-3.99V)

Without this, an SDCC2 (microSD) node whose vmmc/vqmmc point at
vreg_l13b/vreg_l23b probe-defers forever. The SD rails (l13/l23) are the
verified need; the range-struct choice for the other rails is inferred from
the configured DT windows and should be datasheet-confirmed before they are
relied on by other consumers.

supply-name strings are per-rail placeholders (the board DT declares no
parent input supplies for this PMIC), so they are cosmetic here; set the real
vdd-*-supply groupings when the PMIC input schematic is known.

